<http://www.spektrix.com/sidwilliams/event/210401ALGCJGCTKGDHHDSPHPTLLTVVNDB> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Completely Creedence Band - A Tribute to CCR";
  schema:description """
	<span class=\"BoldText\">COMPLETELY CREEDENCE BAND – A TRIBUTE TO CCR</span> <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">THE VOICE. THE SOUND. THE LEGENDARY MUSIC OF CCR.</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Get ready for an electrifying night of classic rock as Completely Creedence brings the unforgettable music of Creedence Clearwater Revival and John Fogerty to life! <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>From <span class=\"ItalicText\">Proud Mary and Bad Moon Rising to Fortunate Son, Green River and Have You Ever Seen the Rain</span>, Completely Creedence delivers the timeless hits that became the soundtrack to a generation. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Fronted by <span class=\"BoldText\">Jamie Robertson</span>, whose remarkable vocals capture the unmistakable sound and spirit of John Fogerty, the band features an exceptional lineup of seasoned musicians:  <span class=\"BoldText\">Murray Atkinson </span> (lead guitar),  <span class=\"BoldText\">Lance Lapointe </span> (bass) and  <span class=\"BoldText\">Grant Baird </span> (drums). <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Together, they deliver powerful musicianship, rich harmonies and the driving rhythms that made CCR legendary. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Since 2015, Completely Creedence Band has entertained audiences throughout British Columbia, earning a loyal following through authentic, high-energy performances and an incredible connection with audiences. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>More than a tribute, it's a celebration of the music, memories and timeless rock and roll that continues to bring generations together. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span> <span class=\"BoldText\">Get ready to sing along, relive the memories and experience the music of CCR – LIVE! <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The Music Lives On. </span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2027-02-04T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/sidwilliams/files/90a5fdfd-ced1-4d6d-a844-5128e6661fdb.jpeg>;
