<http://www.spektrix.com/sidwilliams/event/203001ABHNBGMHRNHHBJRSNLRDJVBPNPM> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Symphony at the Sid: Aretha, Whitney and Tina!";
  schema:description """
	Vancouver Island Symphony’s own Principal Bass Trombonist, Scott MacInnes, takes to the podium as love takes centre stage as the Symphony joins forces with powerhouse vocalist Sonia Reid for an unforgettable Valentine’s celebration inspired by the queens of soul. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Through the iconic music of Aretha Franklin, Whitney Houston, and Tina Turner, this concert wraps audiences in the passion, vulnerability, and joy that defined these legendary voices. From heart‑stopping ballads to electrifying anthems, it’s an evening of pure heart and soul and unforgettable power.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">GUEST CONDUCTOR: Scott MacInnes <span><br/></span>GUEST VOCALIST: Sonia Reid</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Find out more about the Vancouver Island Symphony from their website: <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://https://vancouverislandsymphony.com/\">vancouverislandsymphony.com</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">GET THE SERIES!</span><span><br/></span>3-Concert Series available including:<span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Mischief, Madness & Mystery, Winter Glow and Aretha, Whitney & Tina!</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>You also have the option to add <span class=\"ItalicText\">The Celtic Tenors</span>, a special Vancouver Island Symphony presentation, to the 3-Concert Series Package!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Click on any Vancouver Island Symphony Event, then click the white button that says \"GET EVENT PACKAGES.\" From there, you have the option to click the black button that says \"GET THE SERIES PLUS THE CELTIC TENORS\" or stick with the 3-concert series by clicking \"GET TICKETS.\" <span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Reminder:</span> you will be asked to \"Enter the number of packages you wish to purchase.\" Here, click the small arrow in the text box until you see the number of tickets you would like PER EVENT (for example: if you select \"2\" that means you want 2 tickets to <span class=\"ItalicText\">each</span> series event.) <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Series packages available for a limited time. 
""";
